course: dictionary
lesson: 1644
title: Chilli: one word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. Read the words around the word: they are its context, and they leave clues. «Chilli» is a good example.
explain: «A chilli makes a chemical that tricks your mouth into feeling fire.» The sentence says a chilli is something a plant makes, and that it makes your mouth burn, so a chilli must be a small pepper. Ask: what would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: «Chilli powder» and «sweet chilli sauce» use the same word in a different way. The context shows that chilli can be a spice or an ingredient, not only a pepper on a plant. Both spellings are correct: chilli in UK English and chili in US English.
fact: A chilli is a small pepper, often red or green, that tastes very hot and spicy.
fact: Chilli, or chilli con carne, is a spicy dish made with minced meat, beans, tomatoes and chillies.
fact: Chilli powder or flakes are dried, ground chillies used as a spice.
fact: Chillies came from the Americas and spread around the world. Today they are used in Indian, Mexican, Thai, Chinese and Korean food.
fact: Wash your hands after cutting chillies and never rub your eyes. If your mouth burns, milk soothes it better than water.
exercise: «A chilli makes a chemical that tricks your mouth into feeling fire.» In this sentence, what is a chilli? | A market where grasshoppers are sold | A kind of cold drink | A tall tree | *A small pepper that tastes very hot
exercise: What is chilli powder? | A kind of bean | *Dried, ground chillies used as a spice | Warm water served in a cup | Fresh chillies cut into rings for a salad
exercise: In «chilli con carne», what is the dish made with? | Rice and coffee | *Minced meat, beans, tomatoes and chillies | Grasshoppers and lime | Only sugar and chocolate
test: Chillies came from which part of the world? | Africa | Europe | *The Americas | Australia
test: A mouth burning from chilli feels better after drinking what? | *Milk | Hot tea | Lemonade | Ice-cold water
exam: In «sweet chilli sauce», what does chilli most likely tell you? | A kind of fish | A dance | *A hot, spicy ingredient in the sauce | A type of cold drink
